  "runner_up_case": "The strongest honest case for TRUE is that the claim's operative content — Warren Buffett handing Berkshire Hathaway's leadership to Greg Abel — is confirmed by the best evidence that exists: an SEC Form 8-K recording the board's unanimous May 4, 2025 vote to appoint Abel President and CEO effective January 1, 2026, and Berkshire's own September 18, 2026 press release, which styles him 'Greg Abel, Chief Executive Officer.' Abel did replace Buffett as CEO on January 1, 2026, precisely on the announced schedule, and indisputably ran the company through 2026: Reuters, Britannica, PBS and Business Insider all describe him as Buffett's successor, and Barron's and Business Insider report his first acquisition as CEO. Read as the standard shorthand for that succession — Abel taking over the top job that Buffett held as chairman and CEO — the claim is accurate in substance and fully accurate in its CEO half, which is the half with real operational meaning. The only contested element is the chairman title, and even that was framed from the start as transitional: the May 2025 8-K retained the chairmanship with Buffett only pending the handoff, and on September 18, 2026 the chairmanship left Buffett entirely (to Howard G. Buffett, not Abel). If the analyst's assertion is judged on the CEO succession it describes, every verdict-deciding fact checks out against primary sources and the verdict would be TRUE; MIXED survives only because of the chairman half, which the primary record contradicts.",
  "would_flip_it": [
    "Any Berkshire Hathaway SEC filing (8-K, DEF 14A proxy, or 10-K signature page) or official press release showing Greg Abel elected to or serving as 'Chairman of the Board' on or before 2026-10-01 — e.g., a January 2026 8-K reporting that Abel, not Warren Buffett, assumed the chairmanship when the CEO transition took effect, contradicting the May 2025 8-K's statement that Buffett would remain chairman.",
    "An authentic Berkshire Hathaway press release or 8-K dated on or after September 18, 2026 naming Greg Abel — rather than Howard G. Buffett — as Chairman of the Board, or a correction/superseding announcement showing the September 18 release (sep1826.pdf) did not take effect as reported.",
    "Berkshire Hathaway's corporate governance or leadership page, or its most recent proxy statement, listing Greg Abel as Chairman and CEO as of late September 2026.",
